{% comment %}
  Therapy flow — post-request success screen (node 539:2222), shown after
  "Submit Request" is tapped on Therapy Details (Step 2 of 2). Analogous
  to the consultation flow's Booking Confirmed screen, but simpler and
  genuinely different content, not a restyle of it:
  - Heading is "Request received" (was "Request sent"), subtext now
    "Our care team will call you within 24 hours to fix a session time."
    (was "A confirmation is sent to your WhatsApp number.") — matches a
    later Figma export.
  - A cream-tinted hero band (.kal-step-therapy-confirmed__hero) now
    wraps the success icon/heading/subtext, same overlap technique as
    Booking Confirmed's own mint hero (.kal-step-booking-confirmed__hero)
    — margin-bottom negative so its bottom edge tucks under the card
    below instead of stopping flush above it. Different tint (#fbf6ee
    cream vs Booking Confirmed's #eef3f0 mint), per that export.
  - New "Awaiting callback" pill under the subtext (tan border/text, white
    fill) — replaces this pass's lack of any status indicator here.
  - The old "Consultation Details" list (Reference No./Patient Name/
    Therapy/Payment) is GONE, replaced by a "What happens next" card: a
    3-step vertical timeline (Request sent → Care team calls you →
    Session confirmed), the first step shown completed (filled green
    circle + checkmark, today's timestamp), the second as the current/
    next step (tan-bordered circle + phone icon), the third plain/
    upcoming (grey circle + calendar icon) — same visual language as
    Concern Select's "Your Progress" stepper, but its own dedicated
    classes (.kal-therapy-next-steps__*) since this is a fixed 3-item
    timeline of what happens after submitting, not a 5-step flow
    tracker, and needs its own current_step-less markup.
  - Two action buttons below the card, "Shop Products" and
    "Get directions" — unchanged from before this pass.
  - Header is just a close button, right-aligned — no back button, no
    facility badge, no progress bar (matches the export; also matches
    Booking Confirmed's own "nothing to go back to" reasoning).

  Reuses the shared .kal-confirmation-success-icon/__inner (green
  checkmark badge) from Booking Confirmed's screen — already generic, not
  step-scoped. .kal-confirmation-details__* is no longer used on this
  screen (the list it styled is gone), but stays defined for Booking
  Confirmed's own Video Consult-era usage elsewhere.

  "Request sent"/timestamp and the second/third timeline steps' copy are
  static mockup values, same "visual match, not wired" treatment used
  elsewhere in this flow — no backend call actually schedules a callback
  or produces a real timestamp. Patient Name previously reused
  data-kal-confirm-name on the old details list; that hook has no
  matching element on this screen anymore (harmless no-op, same pattern
  as other now-unused data-kal-confirm-* hooks elsewhere in this flow).

  "Shop Products"/"Get directions" have no click handlers — decorative
  per this build's scope, same as several other action-shaped buttons
  elsewhere in this flow before their real destinations existed.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-therapy-confirmed kal-step-shell">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
      <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">Request sent</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">A confirmation is sent to your WhatsApp number.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-step-entry__location">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
        <!-- ICON: location-pin (not received yet) -->
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
        Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Indiranagar
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    <div class="kal-step-therapy-confirmed__header">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-close aria-label="Close">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'close' -%}
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      {%- comment -%}
        Plain block-flow wrapper (no display:flex), same reason as
        Booking Confirmed's own .kal-step-booking-confirmed__summary —
        .kal-step-shell__scroll's own flex gap would otherwise land
        between the hero and the "What happens next" card below it too,
        eating into the intended overlap. The hero's own negative
        margin-bottom is what makes the card visually tuck under/hover
        over its rounded bottom edge instead of sitting flush below it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-step-therapy-confirmed__summary">
        {%- comment -%}
          Cream hero band (node 539:2222) — wraps icon/heading/subtext/
          badge, same overlap technique as Booking Confirmed's own mint
          hero (margin-bottom negative, tucking its bottom edge under the
          "What happens next" card below instead of stopping flush above
          it).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="kal-step-therapy-confirmed__hero">
          <div class="kal-confirmation-success-icon">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-success-icon__inner">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="kal-step-therapy-confirmed__intro">
            <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Request received</h2>
            <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__subtext">Our care team will call you within 24 hours to fix a session time.</p>
            <span class="kal-therapy-awaiting-badge">Awaiting callback</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          "What happens next" (node 539:2222) — replaces the old
          "Consultation Details" list (Reference No./Patient Name/Therapy/
          Payment) entirely. Fixed 3-step timeline, not tied to any real
          backend state — "Request sent"/timestamp is the only step that's
          actually true right now (this screen only shows once the request
          has been submitted), the other two are what happens next per the
          export, same static-mockup treatment as this flow's other
          decorative status content.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Reuses the exact same stepper classes as Concern Select's "Your
          Progress" (.kal-concern-select__stepper*,
          kal-booking-flow-step-progress.liquid) for pixel-for-pixel the
          same look — circle size/colors, label/state typography, divider
          styling — rather than a parallel set of near-duplicate classes.
          Unlike that 5-step flow tracker, this is a fixed 3-item list
          with no current_step param and no state that ever changes once
          rendered (this screen only shows after the request is already
          submitted), so the --completed/--current modifiers are just
          hardcoded per item instead of computed from a loop.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="kal-therapy-next-steps">
          <p class="kal-therapy-next-steps__label">What happens next</p>
          <ol class="kal-concern-select__stepper">
            <li class="kal-concern-select__stepper-step kal-concern-select__stepper-step--completed">
              <div class="kal-concern-select__stepper-row">
                <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-number">
                  {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
                </span>
                <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-text">
                  <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-label">Request sent</span>
                  <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-state">Today, 4:12 PM</span>
                </span>
              </div>
              <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </li>
            <li class="kal-concern-select__stepper-step kal-concern-select__stepper-step--current">
              <div class="kal-concern-select__stepper-row">
                <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-number">
                  {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'phone' -%}
                </span>
                <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-text">
                  <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-label">Care team calls you</span>
                  <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-state">Within 24 hours</span>
                </span>
              </div>
              <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </li>
            <li class="kal-concern-select__stepper-step">
              <div class="kal-concern-select__stepper-row">
                <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-number">
                  {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'calendar-days' -%}
                </span>
                <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-text">
                  <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-label">Session confirmed</span>
                  <span class="kal-concern-select__stepper-state">Details on WhatsApp</span>
                </span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Visit details card (node 539:2222) — now the exact same
        bordered card the consultation flow's Confirmation step uses
        (.kal-confirmation-appointment-card, reused as-is: photo/
        eyebrow/name header, then icon+label rows below), not a plain
        rows-only card. Eyebrow reads "Therapy Details" instead of
        "Your Consultation"; rows are Patient/Location/Payment instead
        of Mode/Date & Time/Patient. Patient reuses the exact same
        data-kal-confirm-name hook the rest of this flow already
        populates; the doctor photo/name and Location/Payment are
        static mockup values, same "visual match, not wired" treatment
        as elsewhere in this build (no doctor is actually assigned to a
        therapy request, and there's no facility-switcher/payment-method
        step in the therapy flow to reflect a real choice from).

        Kept as a sibling of .kal-step-therapy-confirmed__summary rather
        than nested inside a shared "cards" wrapper with "What happens
        next" and the actions row below — same restructure Booking
        Confirmed's own screen went through: each card is its own flex
        child of .kal-step-shell__scroll, picking up that container's
        24px gap for spacing instead of a wrapper div, with its own
        scoped side-inset/max-width in CSS.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Photo removed per explicit instruction (flow-wide) — same
        .kal-appointment-card__photo--placeholder treatment as the
        Confirmation step's own copy of this card.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card">
        <div class="kal-appointment-card kal-confirmation-appointment-card__top">
          <span class="kal-appointment-card__photo kal-appointment-card__photo--placeholder"></span>
          <span class="kal-appointment-card__body">
            <span class="kal-appointment-card__eyebrow">Therapy Details</span>
            <span class="kal-appointment-card__name">Dr. Neethu Jayachandran</span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__rows">
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'user' -%}
              Patient
            </span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-name>&mdash;</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'location-pin' -%}
              Location
            </span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value">Indiranagar, Bengaluru</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'credit-card' -%}
              Payment
            </span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value">At the clinic</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions">
        <button type="button" class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions__btn">
          <span class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions__icon">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'shopping-cart' -%}
          </span>
          <span>Shop Products</span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions__btn">
          <span class="kal-therapy-confirmed-actions__icon">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'directions' -%}
          </span>
          <span>Get directions</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
